IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`

-- Employment Insurance Regulations (SOR/96-332), piece er6: the nouns shared by the modules of this piece.
-- Text: the plain-text rendering of the Justice Laws consolidation current to 2026-09-30 (SOR-96-332.txt).
-- It is an unofficial conversion; nothing here claims to be verified against the official text.
--
-- WHAT IS HERE: only types, no rules. They come from Schedule I of the Regulations (the regions), which Schedules II.1,
-- II.6, II.8, II.91 and II.92 then list. Every name begins `er6`, as the keel's conventions ask of a piece's types.
-- Other nouns of this piece (the editions of the classification, the units of reg 94) sit in the module that uses them.
-- Nothing here changes the core: the core's vocabulary (`Reason for benefits`, `Rate band`, `Period of days`, ...) is used as it is.

§ `Schedule I -- provinces and territories, census areas, and the place a region is tested against`

-- The headings of Schedule I are the provinces and territories whose regions it lists.
-- src:1769 | Ontario
-- src:1809 | Quebec
-- src:1835 | Nova Scotia
-- src:1843 | New Brunswick
-- src:1864 | Manitoba
-- src:1873 | British Columbia
-- src:1884 | Prince Edward Island
-- src:1888 | Saskatchewan
-- src:1900 | Alberta
-- src:1909 | Newfoundland
-- src:1915 | Yukon
-- src:1919 | Northwest Territories
-- src:1923 | Nunavut
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations Schedule I, the headings over ss 2 to 14 (src:1769-1923)
DECLARE `er6 Province or territory` IS ONE OF
    `er6 Ontario`
    `er6 Quebec`
    `er6 Nova Scotia`
    `er6 New Brunswick`
    `er6 Manitoba`
    `er6 British Columbia`
    `er6 Prince Edward Island`
    `er6 Saskatchewan`
    `er6 Alberta`
    `er6 Newfoundland`
    `er6 Yukon`
    `er6 Northwest Territories`
    `er6 Nunavut`

-- src:1764 | Census Metropolitan Area means a census metropolitan area within the meaning of the Statistics Canada document entitled Standard Geographical Classification (SGC) 1996. (région métropolitaine de recensement)
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations Schedule I s 1 "Census Metropolitan Area" (src:1764)
DECLARE `er6 Census Metropolitan Area or none` IS ONE OF
    `er6 Ottawa — Hull CMA`
    `er6 Oshawa CMA`
    `er6 Toronto CMA`
    `er6 Hamilton CMA`
    `er6 St. Catharines — Niagara CMA`
    `er6 London CMA`
    `er6 Windsor CMA`
    `er6 Kitchener CMA`
    `er6 Sudbury CMA`
    `er6 Thunder Bay CMA`
    `er6 Quebec City CMA`
    `er6 Trois-Rivières CMA`
    `er6 Sherbrooke CMA`
    `er6 Montreal CMA`
    `er6 Chicoutimi — Jonquière CMA`
    `er6 Halifax CMA`
    `er6 Saint John CMA`
    `er6 Winnipeg CMA`
    `er6 Vancouver CMA`
    `er6 Victoria CMA`
    `er6 Regina CMA`
    `er6 Saskatoon CMA`
    `er6 Calgary CMA`
    `er6 Edmonton CMA`
    `er6 St. John’s CMA`
    `er6 no Census Metropolitan Area`

-- src:1762 | Census Agglomeration for the purposes of sections 2, 5, 7 and 9, means a census agglomeration within the meaning of the Statistics Canada document entitled Standard Geographical Classification (SGC) 1996 and for the purposes of sections 8, 12 and 13, means a census agglomeration within the meaning of the Statistics Canada document entitled Standard Geographical Classification (SGC) 2011. (agglomération de recensement)
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations Schedule I s 1 "Census Agglomeration" (src:1762)
DECLARE `er6 Census Agglomeration or none` IS ONE OF
    `er6 Kingston CA`
    `er6 Moncton CA`
    `er6 Fredericton CA`
    `er6 Abbotsford CA`
    `er6 North Battleford CA`
    `er6 Charlottetown CA`
    `er6 Whitehorse CA`
    `er6 Yellowknife CA`
    `er6 no Census Agglomeration`

-- A PLACE is what Schedule I tests: it describes a region by what it consists of (census divisions, census
-- subdivisions, metropolitan areas and agglomerations), so the person is described by where they live in those terms.
-- The numbers are Statistics Canada's Standard Geographical Classification numbers, each as the Schedule writes it:
-- a census division number is the two-digit number within the province (so "Census Division No. 11" means a
-- different division in each province and every region rule also tests the province, as the heading above its section
-- does); a census subdivision number is the full code in New Brunswick and Nunavut and the five-digit code
-- (census division and subdivision, "01557") in Newfoundland. The edition of the classification is the one Schedule I s 1 names
-- for the section being applied (the 1996 edition for most, the 2011 edition for the agglomeration of ss 8, 12 and 13
-- and for the subdivisions of ss 8 and 12 to 14); the person states each fact in that edition.
-- The last field is not a classification at all: s 2(9)(b) divides Census Division No. 34 by whether it "lies east of" the
-- Census Metropolitan Area of London, and nothing else in the Schedule says where that line is, so it is a fact about the place.
-- src:1762 | Census Agglomeration for the purposes of sections 2, 5, 7 and 9, means a census agglomeration within the meaning of the Statistics Canada document entitled Standard Geographical Classification (SGC) 1996 and for the purposes of sections 8, 12 and 13, means a census agglomeration within the meaning of the Statistics Canada document entitled Standard Geographical Classification (SGC) 2011. (agglomération de recensement)
-- src:1763 | Census Division means a census division within the meaning of the Statistics Canada document entitled Standard Geographical Classification (SGC) 1996. (division de recensement)
-- src:1764 | Census Metropolitan Area means a census metropolitan area within the meaning of the Statistics Canada document entitled Standard Geographical Classification (SGC) 1996. (région métropolitaine de recensement)
-- src:1765 | Census Subdivision for the purposes of sections 5 and 11, means a census subdivision within the meaning of the Statistics Canada document entitled Standard Geographical Classification (SGC) 1996 and for the purposes of sections 8 and 12 to 14, means a census subdivision within the meaning of the Statistics Canada document entitled Standard Geographical Classification (SGC) 2011. (subdivision de recensement)
-- src:1792 | (b) the portion of Census Division No. 34 that lies east of and is not part of the Census Metropolitan Area of London; and
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations Schedule I s 1 (src:1762-1765) and s 2(9)(b) (src:1792)
DECLARE `er6 Place` HAS
    `province or territory`                          IS AN `er6 Province or territory`
    `census division`                                IS A NUMBER
    `census subdivision`                             IS A NUMBER
    `census metropolitan area`                       IS AN `er6 Census Metropolitan Area or none`
    `census agglomeration`                           IS AN `er6 Census Agglomeration or none`
    `east of the Census Metropolitan Area of London` IS A BOOLEAN

